    <div class="quiz-question" data-correct="0">
      <p>What is the primary strategic advantage of RAG over fine-tuning an LLM?</p>
      <ul class="quiz-options">
        <li>A) It grounds answers in source documents and allows knowledge updates without retraining</li>
        <li>B) It always produces faster inference than fine-tuned models</li>
        <li>C) It eliminates the need for an embedding model</li>
        <li>D) It guarantees the LLM will never hallucinate</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="quiz-answer">RAG's key advantage is grounding and updatability. You can update your document corpus without retraining the LLM. Fine-tuning is expensive and slow; RAG scales to handle knowledge updates in hours. Note: RAG doesn't eliminate hallucination entirely and may introduce retrieval latency.</div>
